{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And his flux.</b> A term of spittle — his flesh fluxes its flux like spittle, that comes out clear." "<b>Or that blocks.</b> That comes out thick, and stops up the opening of the member, and his flesh is stopped from the drip of his flux — this is its plain sense. And its midrash: the verse counts the first, two sightings, and calls him impure, as it says, ״a man who has a flux from his flesh — his flux is impure״; and the verse counts the second, three sightings, and calls him impure, as it says, ״his impurity — by his flux: his flesh fluxed its flux, or his flesh was blocked from his flux, it is his impurity.״ How so? Two bring impurity, and the third obligates him for a sacrifice (Niddah 43a; Megillah 8a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:32.668386306Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}